The only query that computes the tip percentage the same way the specification (and the provided “External knowledge” section) defines it—tip % = tip / (pre‑tip total) × 100—is 0result.sql.  
Queries 1result.sql (uses tip / total) and 2result.sql (uses tip / fare_amount) apply a different denominator, so their bucket assignments and proportions are wrong.  
Hence, 0result.sql is the correct choice.

```plaintext
0result.sql
```